:root {

--bg: #faf8f3; --text: #2c2418; --accent: #8b6914; --accent-muted: #b8a070;

--border: #d4c9a8; --translator-bg: #eef3ed; --translator-border: #7a9a6d;

--subtitle-bg: #f5f0e0; --section-num: #6b5a2a;

* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

body {

background-color: var(--bg); color: var(--text);

font-family: 'EB Garamond', 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;

font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.85; padding: 2rem 1rem;

max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: justify;

.book-title { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }

.halacha-title { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 1.8rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); }

.lm-subtitle { background-color: #f8f4e8; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; border-radius: 4px; text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: var(--section-num); }

.paragraph { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

.verse { font-style: italic; color: #4a3b1f; }

.source-ref { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--accent-muted); font-style: normal; }

.heb-term { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }

.heb-def { font-size: 0.9rem; color: #6a5a3a; }

.lm-ref { font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); }

.key-concept { font-weight: 600; }

.maxim { font-weight: 600; color: #4a3b1f; font-style: italic; }

.translator-summary { background-color: var(--translator-bg); border: 1px solid var(--translator-border); border-left: 5px solid var(--translator-border); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }

.translator-summary .summary-heading { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--translator-border); margin-bottom: 0.8rem; text-align: center; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }

Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim

Hilchos Netilas Yadayim L'Seudah U'Betzi'as HaPas 2

Based on the discourse of Rabbainu, may his light shine,

(Likutay Moharan I, 44) — concerning the clapping of hands, which serves to purify the air in the aspect of Eretz Yisrael, through the power of the joints of the hands, through which the "power of His deeds" is aroused.

For it is found in the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine (Likutay Moharan I, 44), concerning the clapping of hands [mechi'as kaf] — that it serves to purify the air in the aspect of Eretz Yisrael, through the ko'ach pirkin d'yadayim [the power of the joints of the hands], through which the "power of His deeds" [ko'ach ma'asav] is aroused — for the primary holiness of Eretz Yisrael comes through this — see there. And through this, one is saved from confusing thoughts, which are the aspect of mabul [the Flood], the aspect of bilbul [confusion]. And through drawing down the holiness of Eretz Yisrael, one is saved from the aspect of the mabul — for in Eretz Yisrael, there was no Flood — see there well.
